==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
-

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Once the first Metal Hippoe is gone, the stage is easily rushable by the likes of [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]. Bring a reliable [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critter]] ([[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] works wonders) and something to Z-Kill the Znaches, like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], and you'll be all set. Watch out for their Burrow, as if they sneak behind your Cats and you've hit the deploy limit, there's basically nothing you can do except hope your units destroy the enemy base before the Znaches get yours.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
You can brute force this stage relatively easily with a combination of various piercing attackers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] alongside a few Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s.

Simply kill the Thrillerz at the start with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]], then use Jelly Dumpling Cat in combination with [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] to kill Sir Rel. You should have enough cash to afford Bahamut and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]. At this point, it's just a matter of occasionally meatshielding with [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cats]].

Awakened Bahamut Cat and Jelly Dumpling Cat will chip down and knock back Corporal Weyland, while Cat Researcher hopefully picks up the slack with a few Critical Hits on the Metal Hippoes. If all goes well, the stage should be over and done with just like that.

